Package: timeProtState
Type: Package
Title: Contrast-Aware Pathway Remodeling Dynamics for Time-Course Proteomics
Version: 0.99.0
Date: 2026-09-21
Authors@R: c(
    person(given = "Weile", family = "Xie",
           email = "weile.xie@outlook.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre")))
Description: Provides an auditable framework for shared-baseline,
    multi-condition time-course proteomics experiments. The package
    constructs estimable contrast families from a saturated group-means
    design (shared-baseline contrast grammar), decomposes protein-level
    temporal and condition-dependent evidence into transparent axes, and
    reports pathway NET, REM, and COH summaries. Pathway significance
    uses limma CAMERA for independent arrays or ROMER when a
    repeat-measures block is set. Optional repeated-measures correlation
    is supported in the fit. Includes trajectory clustering,
    correlated-pathway simulation for benchmarks, and structured export.
